    "summary": {
      "value": "Extend single-target spells."
    },
    "description": "<p><strong>Requirements:</strong> you must have mastered <strong>Loremaster</strong>.</p><hr><p>When you cast a spell with a <strong>target</strong> of “One creature”, you may choose an Attribute (<strong>Dexterity</strong>, <strong>Insight</strong>, <strong>Might</strong>, or <strong>Willpower</strong>) and a die size (<strong>d6</strong>, <strong>d8</strong>, <strong>d10</strong>, or <strong>d12</strong>). If you do, the spell's <strong>target</strong> becomes “Every creature present on the scene whose <strong>current</strong> die size in that Attribute matches your choice” and its <strong>total Mind Point cost is doubled</strong>. Additionally, all mentions of “the target” in the spell's text are replaced with “each target”; or they are replaced with “one or more targets” if the spell is <strong>Anomaly</strong>, <strong>Dispel</strong>, <strong>Mercy</strong>, or <strong>Mirror</strong>. When the spell ends on one or more of its targets, it automatically ends on all its targets.</p><p>If you cast an offensive spell (@ICON[offensive]) this way, you perform a single Magic Check and compare it with the Magic Defense of each target.</p>",
